  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a **hotel conversion** in the Caribbean and Latin America, owners commonly look at **soft-brand** and **collection** options such as Marriott’s **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, **The Luxury Collection**, and sometimes **Delta Hotels** or **Four Points by Sheraton** for conversion-friendly positioning.[2][3]\n\nOther frequently considered soft-brand/collection-style options in the region include IHG’s **Vignette Collection** and **Voco**, which are specifically described as attractive for owners seeking recognition and flexibility without creating a fully new identity.[7]\n\nIf you mean the broader regional market rather than just Marriott and IHG, Hyatt’s **Inclusive Collection** brands such as **Sunscape**, **Dreams**, **Hyatt Ziva**, and **Hyatt Zilara** are also active in Caribbean and Latin America conversions, especially for all-inclusive assets.[5]",
